## 7. Hardest Problems — Final Ranking

| # | Problem | Why Hard | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Closing the feedback loop** | Zone outcomes must auto-write feature vectors to Supabase at trade entry — if this breaks, XGBoost has nothing to train on | Phase 4 |
| 2 | **RAGFlow integration** | Another service to run, maintain, and query from LangGraph. Table parsing for financial statements is non-trivial | Phase 3 |
| 3 | **LangGraph checkpointing** | PostgresSaver requires direct DB connection (not REST API), schema setup, and careful state design | Phase 0 |
| 4 | **Temporal awareness in retrieval** | Every RAG query needs timestamp filtering or you get stale macro context | Phase 3 |
| 5 | **Event-driven scheduler** | VIX thresholds, earnings dates, FOMC calendar — needs a proper event bus | Phase 2 |
| 6 | **Gemma 4 local fine-tuning** | LoRA training on zone outcome data — needs 500+ records first | Phase 8 |
| 7 | **Multi-agent race conditions** | Concurrent Supabase writes need atomic upserts + DAG-enforced execution order | Throughout |

